The earlier count of 15 included factor pairs of opposite parity, which do not yield integer \(x,y\). Writing  
\((x-y)(x+y)=720\), both factors must be even since their product is even and they must have the same parity. Divide by 4: if \(x-y=2m\), \(x+y=2n\), then \(mn=180\) with \(n>m\). Since \(180\) has \(18\) divisors and is not a square, there are \(18/2=9\) valid pairs.

